{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "sectional-anatomy",
    "title": "Sectional Anatomy",
    "order": 11
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "foundations",
    "title": "Sectional Anatomy: Foundations",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Reading a Cross-Section \u2014 The Three Planes",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every image a therapist reviews at the console is a slice through the body in one of three planes. Reading them fluently is the foundation of both contouring and daily setup verification."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Plane"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Divides the body into"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "What you see"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Axial (transverse)",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Superior / inferior"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "A \"doughnut\" slice viewed from the patient's feet \u2014 the patient's right is on the "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "left",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "italic"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": " of your screen (radiologic convention)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Coronal",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Anterior / posterior"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "A front-facing slice, like looking at the patient standing before you"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Sagittal",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Left / right"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "A side-profile slice; the midsagittal plane splits the body into equal halves"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "radiologic convention",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " for axial images (patient's right on the viewer's left) is why a right-lung tumor appears on the left of your screen. Getting this backwards is one of the most consequential orientation errors in the department."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Couch Movements and Image Planes",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Each plane corresponds to a physical couch or scan axis, which is exactly how a therapist translates an image shift into a table move:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Axial stack \u2192 longitudinal (in/out).",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Scrolling through axial slices moves you superior\u2013inferior, the same axis as the couch's long travel."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Vertical (up/down)",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " and "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "lateral (left/right)",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " couch moves reposition the patient within the coronal and sagittal planes."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "When a verification image shows the target 5 mm too inferior, the correction is a longitudinal couch shift \u2014 the plane you saw the error in tells you which axis to move."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "f_p2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "On a standard axial CT slice viewed in radiologic convention, where does a structure in the patient's "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "right",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " lung appear?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "On the left side of the viewer's screen",
              "On the right side of the viewer's screen"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Axial images are conventionally displayed as if looking up from the patient's feet, so the patient's right is on the viewer's left. Reversing this flips laterality \u2014 a critical setup error."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "The Hounsfield Scale",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "CT numbers are reported in "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Hounsfield Units (HU)",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ", a scale anchored so that "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "water = 0 HU",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "air = \u22121000 HU",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": ". Every tissue sits at a characteristic value, which is what lets you identify a structure by its brightness before you even recognize its shape."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Tissue"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Approximate HU"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Air (lung)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "\u22121000 (\u2212500 in aerated lung)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Fat"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "\u2212100 to \u221250"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Water"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "0"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Soft tissue / muscle"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "+20 to +80"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Cortical bone"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "+400 to +1000+"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "In treatment planning, HU values also feed the dose calculation directly \u2014 the planning system converts CT number to electron density, which is why an accurate, artifact-free simulation scan matters for more than just contouring."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "f_p3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "On the Hounsfield scale, what value is assigned to water?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "\u22121000 HU",
              "0 HU",
              "+1000 HU"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The scale is defined with water at 0 HU and air at \u22121000 HU. Bone runs strongly positive; fat is mildly negative."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Window Width and Window Level",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A CT holds far more grayscale range than a monitor or the eye can display at once, so the image is "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "windowed",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " to show the tissues of interest:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Window Level (WL)",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 the center HU value of the displayed range (sets overall brightness)."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Window Width (WW)",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 the range of HU spread across black-to-white (sets contrast). A "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "narrow",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "italic"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " width gives high contrast over a small HU band; a "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "wide",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "italic"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " width shows more tissues but flatter contrast."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Window preset"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Reveals"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Lung window (wide WW, low WL)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Lung parenchyma, airways, pneumothorax"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Soft-tissue / mediastinal window"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Organs, vessels, nodal disease"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Bone window (very wide WW)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Cortex, trabeculae, lytic/blastic lesions"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Brain window (narrow WW)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Gray\u2013white differentiation, edema, hemorrhage"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "This is why the same thoracic slice must be read on "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "both",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "italic"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " lung and mediastinal windows \u2014 each reveals a tissue interface the other hides."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "From Diagnostic Image to Daily Verification",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Sectional anatomy underpins two core radiation-therapy tasks:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "orderedList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Contouring & localization",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " at simulation \u2014 the target and organs at risk are drawn slice by slice on the planning CT."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Daily anatomic verification",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " at the machine \u2014 before beam-on, the therapist compares in-room imaging against the reference to confirm the anatomy sits where the plan expects."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Image-guided verification generally means matching on one of two things: a "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "bony match",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (aligning skeletal landmarks on kV/kV or CBCT to the DRR) or a "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "soft-tissue match",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (aligning the organ/target itself on CBCT, e.g., prostate or bladder). Knowing which structures are reliable surrogates in each region is the whole point of the lessons that follow."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "f_p5_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A therapist aligns the daily CBCT to the target organ itself (e.g., the prostate) rather than to the pelvic bones. This is best described as a:"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Bony match",
              "Soft-tissue match",
              "Longitudinal-only match"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Matching to the organ/target directly is a soft-tissue match \u2014 important where the target moves independently of bone, as the prostate does relative to the pelvis."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
